  "conclusions": [
    "Both prefix and appended --no-deref forms are accepted by this installed Git. An expected-old-OID update from symref A succeeds, replaces that checkpoint alias with a direct B ref and preserves the tag referent A.",
    "Global --no-deref also applies to --stdin. verify(expected A) accepts the symref and preserves it; update(A to B) accepts the symref and replaces it with a direct B ref.",
    "The corresponding direct-ref verify and update controls succeed normally.",
    "Therefore --no-deref prevents writing through this alias to its referent, but alone does not require or certify a direct ref and does not refuse replacing an unknown alias. Explicit type validation while native ref locks are held is a separate requirement."
  ],
